## This machine is NixOS

Nothing here gets installed with apt, pip or npm -g, and a program missing from `PATH` is not missing: all of nixpkgs is one command away.
{%- if comma %}

- `, <program> <args>` is the shortest way to that. `,` is itself a program (comma): it looks up any nixpkgs package shipping an executable of that name, builds only that one and runs it.

```
, gcc program.c
, rg --version
, python3 -m http.server
```

The leading `,` is the command's real name, not a typo. `,-x <program>` prints the store path instead of running, `,-s <program>` opens a shell with the package loaded.
{%- endif %}
{%- if nix %}

- `nix run nixpkgs#<pkg> -- <args>` runs a package by attribute, `nix build nixpkgs#<pkg>` puts it in `./result`, `nix-shell -p <pkg> --run '<cmd>'` gives a shell with the package and its dependencies.
- `nix search nixpkgs <term>` answers what exists.
{%- endif %}
